Dexed for WebCLAP (open-webclap port): what the browser build changes in Dexed's own sources.

module.wasm is the processor without an editor, so it is compiled with DEXED_HEADLESS; both modules are compiled
with DEXED_WEBCLAP. Neither macro is defined in upstream builds, whose behaviour stays unchanged. The changes:

  - PluginProcessor.h: no clap-juce-extensions (the kit wraps the processor itself); the FileChooser member is
    left out of the headless build.
  - PluginProcessor.cpp: the headless build leaves out the editor include and hasEditor()/createEditor()
    (ports/dexed/dsp_main.cpp defines them), and computes the VU meter decay itself (the same formula as
    VuMeterOutput::getDecayFactor, which belongs to the editor's sources).
  - PluginData.cpp: the headless build shows no AlertWindow. One added `return` after the "Unable to open"
    dialog in sendSysexCartridge: the code went on to dereference the null stream.
  - Tuning.cpp: the FileChooser-driven applySCLTuning() / applyKBMMapping() overloads are left out of the
    headless build (the editor, in the page, owns those menus).
  - msfa/tuning.cc: its seven AlertWindow calls go through one helper that does nothing in the headless build.
  - midi/SysexComm.h: no MidiInput/MidiOutput members (juce_audio_devices is not part of the browser build). The
    device code that would fill them is already disabled upstream ("TODO: refactor this since JUCE 8").

--- a/source/PluginData.cpp
+++ b/source/PluginData.cpp
@@ -150,20 +150,25 @@
     
     std::unique_ptr<juce::FileInputStream> fis = cart.createInputStream();
     if ( fis == NULL ) {
+#ifndef DEXED_HEADLESS // WebCLAP: the DSP module shows no dialogs
         String f = cart.getFullPathName();
         AlertWindow::showMessageBoxAsync (AlertWindow::WarningIcon,
                                           "Error",
                                           "Unable to open: " + f);
+#endif
+        return; // (it dereferenced the null stream below)
     }
     
     uint8 syx_data[65535];
     int sz = fis->read(syx_data, 65535);
     
     if (syx_data[0] != 0xF0) {
+#ifndef DEXED_HEADLESS
         String f = cart.getFullPathName();
         AlertWindow::showMessageBoxAsync (AlertWindow::WarningIcon,
                                           "Error",
                                           "File: " + f + " doesn't seems to contain any sysex data");
+#endif
         return;
     }
     sysexComm.send(MidiMessage(syx_data, sz));
